import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>10.2b — Recursive Traversal: Reverse, Palindrome, and Sum</h1>

<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Recursive String and Array Tools</h3>
        <p>Yesterday you saw how recursion traverses strings and arrays. Today you'll write the classic recursive traversal problems — each one builds on the same pattern.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>RecursiveTools</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Reverse a String</strong> <code>String reverse(String s)</code>:
                <ul>
                    <li>Base case: if length <= 1, return s</li>
                    <li>Recursive: last character + reverse(the rest)</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Palindrome Check</strong> <code>boolean isPalindrome(String s)</code>:
                <ul>
                    <li>Base cases: if length <= 1 → true. If first != last → false.</li>
                    <li>Recursive: check the substring without first and last characters</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Sum Array</strong> <code>int sum(int[] arr, int index)</code>:
                <ul>
                    <li>Base case: index >= arr.length → return 0</li>
                    <li>Recursive: arr[index] + sum(arr, index+1)</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Trace isPalindrome("racecar")</h3>
        <p>Write out every recursive call. At what call does the base case fire? How many total calls are made?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-10/recursion-basics.html">Recursion</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/string.html">String Methods</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
